Description:
Gold Coast TechSpace is a physical place where people come to hack around with and learn about technology, eg software, hardware, robotics, green technology, or anything else that takes your fancy. We are based on the highly successful Hackerspace model, found all over the world, with thousands of groups in the US and several in Australia cities including Brisbane;
 - to attend the various public events, workshops and learning sessions conducted there from time to time;
 - to co-work during the business week.

The range of activities undertaken is entirely determined by our members. We cater for all age groups, including children under parental supervision.

Our aims are to help showcase and promote technology on the Gold Coast at a practical grassroot level, and help ensure our members and the local community can engage in and also gain employment in technology.

Lighting Council Australia is the peak body for Australia's lighting industry. Its goal is to encourage the use of environmentally appropriate, energy efficient, quality lighting systems.

Lighting Council Australia:
- advocates the importance of energy efficient, quality, low environmental impact lighting products and systems;
- represents the Australian lighting industry to policy-makers and other key stakeholders nationally and internationally;
influences international and Australian standards relating to the lighting industry;
- promotes the use of electrically safe lighting that complies with relevant Australian and international standards; and
- encourages good lighting design, education and training.

